          {
            "commit": "71b5903e1d5aba5f3bd8ba2cfe1a788bd76009e8",
            "subject": "LU-10499 pcc: asynchronous PCCRO attach command support"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-18 00:58:33.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-21 19:18:47.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-10499 pcc: DIO attach copy for encrypted files",
        "message": "LU-10499 pcc: DIO attach copy for encrypted files\n\nThe PCC copy of an encrypted file holds its ciphertext, so the\nkernel copy sets S_PCCCOPY to read the Lustre file as if the key\nwere not loaded.  The DIO copy by ll_fid_path_copy was not used for\nencrypted files, since its direct reads would decrypt the data when\nthe key is loaded.\n\nNow that direct IO of a file opened with O_CIPHERTEXT transfers the\nciphertext whether the key is loaded or not, have ll_fid_path_copy\nopen the source file with O_CIPHERTEXT for its direct IO, and use\nthe DIO copy for encrypted files.  O_CIPHERTEXT has no effect on\nthe direct IO of other files, except that its O_NONBLOCK does not\nrestore a released file, whose copy then fails and the kernel falls\nback to the buffered copy.  A ciphertext read reaches the end of the\nlast encryption unit, so the copy may be up to one unit larger than\nthe clear text size, as with the kernel copy.\n\nAdd sanity-pcc test_50d to verify the PCC copy of an encrypted file.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ia3d6809c5e9631d7f375d51d9946fdb3373ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
